{{define "project-microbiome"}}
<div class="nav-bars" id="nav-path" hx-swap-oob="true">
  <div id="nav-path-text">
    {{ template "project-microbiome-path" .}}
  </div>
</div>

<div id="nav-content" hx-history-elt>
  <style>
    #iframe-video {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
  </style>
  <h1>a VST3/AU/LV2 delay-based audio effects plugin</h1>
  <figure class="centered">
    <iframe id="iframe-video" width="560" height="315"
      src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ihh65Blad9o?si=ucj9ccgX-M66WZ-T" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0"
      allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
      referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
    <figcaption>Microbiome Demo</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>What if sound was treated as a breathing, living, entity?</h2>
  <p>
    Microbiome's audio processing engine consists of a number of toggleable <b>colonies</b>. Each colony is an offshoot
    of the original sound source, a resampling of a certain portion of the main audio signal.
    The colonies apply their own processing algorithm to their resampled audio before feeding it back into the output
    signal, resulting in a constantly evolving sound signature that is based off the characteristics of the signal's
    past.
  </p>

  <br>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <figure>
      <a href="/static/images/projects/microbiome_0_enabled.webp" target="_blank">
        <img src="/static/images/projects/microbiome_0_enabled.webp" width="853" height="501" loading="lazy"
          alt="Microbiome editor with Colony #1 disabled">
      </a>
      <figcaption>Figure 1: Colony #1 disabled</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <a href="/static/images/projects/microbiome_1_enabled.webp" target="_blank">
        <img src="/static/images/projects/microbiome_1_enabled.webp" width="852" height="500" loading="lazy"
          alt="Microbiome editor with Colony #1 enabled">
      </a>
      <figcaption>Figure 2: Colony #1 enabled</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="wide">
      <a href="/static/images/projects/microbiome_2_enabled.webp" target="_blank">
        <img src="/static/images/projects/microbiome_2_enabled.webp" width="852" height="501" loading="lazy"
          alt="Microbiome editor with three enabled colonies">
      </a>
      <figcaption>Figure 3: Three enabled colonies at varying resampling seek positions and buffer start/end
        points</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

